      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The scientific consensus is unequivocal that a rapid phase-out of fossil fuels is the only viable path to preventing catastrophic climate change, and this urgency must supersede short-term economic stability concerns. While some policymakers argue for a gradual transition to protect vulnerable economies, delaying action to prioritize immediate economic stability will only result in far greater long-term economic devastation from climate disasters. Governments must prioritize aggressive decarbonization now, accepting the necessary short-term costs to secure a stable future for generations to come.",
      "source": "target",
