      "content": "but even when you're being \"balanced\" now, it feels like you're still leaning one way. you say ignoring economic realities is a \"political choice,\" but then you immediately follow it up by saying the debate is about \"balancing\" them. isn't the real debate actually whether the economic risks are a legitimate reason to slow down, or if they are just an excuse used by fossil fuel interests to delay progress? could you explain why some people see the economic argument as a valid shield for inaction?",
